  message: "DONE on the go half this item turned out to be (PR pending merge; SHA in the follow-up entry).\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. go.yaml rows bufio.Reader.{ReadString,ReadBytes,ReadLine,ReadRune,ReadSlice,Read} and bufio.Scanner.{Scan,Text,Bytes}, dual fs_read/ipc_recv under call_site_undecidable (INV-zumin class (b)), abstains_to fs_read. go.py stamps io_target_kind on the READ by resolving the receiver's last binding back to the wrapper call and classifying that call's argument as WI-lipis's wrapper site does (inline producer directly; bare identifier through one more hop, taken at the WRAPPER's line). Parameter, field, non-wrapper binding, or an unbound argument: no stamp. Reachability probed BEFORE the rows were written (LIVE rule 9): every name reaches from the `bufio` hint, none leaks through a hint-less short name; ambiguous_names unchanged.\n\nWHY fs_read IS THE FALLBACK, the opposite of the constructors'. An unstamped read's receiver came from a scope the analyzer cannot see, and the wrapper that built it lives THERE, where the constructor row already carries the unresolved case's ipc_recv fallback. A second ipc_recv here would double-mint one crossing.\n\nMEASURED, A/B on alertmanager, beads, caddy, cert-manager, cilium, jaeger (arm A finished before any edit; call-edge counts identical per repo; ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/vutav_reads_09032026/, every moved row in ab_compare.out with its receiver's binding recovered from source):\n  179 read sites reach the rows; 0 rows removed; constructors unmoved\n    8 std_stream -> ipc_recv, ALL read back to a local bufio.New*(os.Stdin): beads doctor_fix.go:84/138, doctor_validate.go:157 (prompts); caddy caddyauth/command.go:129 (hash-password plaintext); cilium tools/testowners/main.go:59/62/107/108\n   91 host_path -> fs_read (file handles)\n   41 in_memory -> fs_read at classification, refused as sources at the mint gate\n   39 unstamped -> fs_read: 2 parameter receivers, 9 struct fields, 28 locals whose wrapper argument is a parameter (caddy parseEnvFile(envInput io.Reader), cilium readSchedstat(f io.ReadSeeker), parseMetricsFromProm(promFile io.Reader)), an in-repo wrapper (beads createMarkdownScanner), a pipe, an io.LimitReader, or &buf of a declared bytes.Buffer -- each read back; no missed os.Open\n  Nothing moved on cert-manager or alertmanager (no typed bufio read receivers).\n\nTHE ITEM'S OTHER ARMS, per language, checked through the loader today:\n  python  sys.stdin.{read,readline,readlines} ipc_recv       DONE (before this item)\n  rust    std::io::Stdin.{read_line,lines}     ipc_recv       DONE (before this item)\n  c       stdio.{fgets,fread,...}              dual, stamped  DONE (WI-lipis 3rd deliverable)\n  java    BufferedReader.{readLine,read}, Scanner.nextLine at FIXED fs_read -> a stdin read mints NOTHING. RESIDUAL, filed as a sibling (receiver-origin shape; WI-lipis holds the constructor half).\n  cpp     std::getline ABSENT (c getline too); stream is an ARGUMENT. RESIDUAL, filed as a sibling.\n  go      os.File.Read                          still WI-lalot (producing-function -> type table)\n\nNOT DONE HERE, BY DESIGN: the constructor retag. ADR-0049 ruling 3 now has a represented crossing to relocate to; whether the 0010 arm-2 findings survive the retag is a separate re-run and a separate ruling. bufio.NewReaderSize/NewReadWriter readers are disclosed on the row and stamp nothing."  # ced7
